_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"06dc0c0b7f18d04845d809827320ab6c6f992ddc4d359965d809df5c7f30eca7","event_uuid":"34fca5df-5fad-457b-94dc-de796fb2e88e","position":{"commit_sha":"619db71a273653bbfa70c6eae2516bf967e1c4d7","position":"1787086704484819001-34fca5df-5fad-457b-94dc-de796fb2e88e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"aaf7807a408a0e7f90117623dd2f9d98ab8c828cc80ca168bcfaa5704f5f14ed","event_uuid":"572f8b93-8f78-4ba2-b34f-7b7df448d131","position":{"commit_sha":"77d53fe44a0e899a7db92b710ee7788d00f367b5","position":"1787087293004668001-572f8b93-8f78-4ba2-b34f-7b7df448d131"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"38a48f90313d6e5b36d06274e34e1db1ed144db52cb83fd767fddce75325d6b5","event_uuid":"f2094dd7-2f63-4e55-bb9e-d75693916043","position":{"commit_sha":"6607df77934d39aaa32e7e624cbc0c7d2a643662","position":"1787087313352826001-f2094dd7-2f63-4e55-bb9e-d75693916043"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"90e15552751bf8cad95a66424bd734dbe5f7b3accac87277e223158d94791a45","event_uuid":"055261ce-f082-4cff-902f-9738c0bcb8a9","position":{"commit_sha":"470ed7a5d5a038adbdf15b3c266edbda453083b5","position":"1787087319908510001-055261ce-f082-4cff-902f-9738c0bcb8a9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 confirmed a two-part incomplete implementation in the handwritten MCP adapter. E1 built the real server and inspected both the registered callable and live FastMCP schema in the same process: signature `(id1, id2)` and schema properties `{id1,id2}` both omitted `relation`, ruling out stale client/server cache. E2 drove a real MCP unlink against an ephemeral pair holding `blocks` then `relates_to`: the runtime spy recorded exactly two positional arguments, MCP removed the newest `relates_to` edge, while the library control `rebar.unlink(a,b,\"blocks\")` removed only `blocks`. E3 temporarily added only the optional callable parameter while deliberately leaving the two-argument delegate unchanged: the live schema then accepted `relation=\"blocks\"`, but the spy still recorded only `(a,b)` and MCP still removed `relates_to`; instrumentation was removed and the worktree is clean.\n\nRoot cause: `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets` independently omits the already-supported optional relation selector from both its registered signature and its `rebar.unlink` call. Both omissions are necessary to explain the inability to express the selector and the pair-scoped fallback at runtime. Defect legitimacy is `incomplete-implementation`: the signed final ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish requires zero intended write-parameter divergences and total lib/CLI/MCP parity; relation-scoped unlink is already authoritative in docs/user-guide.md, docs/cli-reference.md, core/library code, and tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_unlink_relation_scoped_e39f.py. The older ticket-model prose and commit 73abb580 only record the earlier change scope, not a permanent divergence. Expected behavior: an explicit MCP relation removes exactly that edge; omission preserves pair-scoped most-recent behavior.","timestamp":1787087293004668001}],"created_at":1787086578886175001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0639fd5b-bf48-4273-b1cb-c9f445abff5b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1128-505b-54ac-497f"}],"description":"## Context\nThe public CLI and Python library support relation-specific unlink so callers can remove exactly one edge when the same ticket pair carries multiple relations. The registered MCP `unlink_tickets` tool accepts only `id1` and `id2` and delegates `rebar.unlink` without `relation`. FastMCP therefore advertises no relation field and execution takes the pair-scoped fallback, removing the most-recent edge rather than the requested edge.\n\nThe signed final write-surface ruling on `restoring-shallow-blobfish` requires total parameter parity across library, CLI, and MCP with zero intended divergences. The earlier relation-scoped change explicitly left MCP outside that change scope, but did not establish a permanent divergence.\n\n## Proven root cause\n`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py::unlink_tickets` independently omits the already-supported optional relation selector from (1) its registered callable signature/live FastMCP schema and (2) its `rebar.unlink` delegate call. Runtime experiments proved both omissions: current MCP forwards only two args and removes the newest relation; a signature-only mutation makes the schema accept `relation` but still loses the value at the delegate.\n\n## Repair plan\n- Add `relation: str | None = None` to the MCP callable, matching the public library contract.\n- Forward `relation` unchanged to `rebar.unlink`.\n- Update the tool description to document explicit relation-scoped removal and the omitted-selector fallback.\n- Add a held-out interface oracle through the real FastMCP registration and real ephemeral ticket store.\n- Preserve pair-scoped most-recent behavior when `relation` is omitted.\n- Sweep the write surfaces and stale unlink documentation for the same parity gap; record or repair each confirmed sibling according to scope.\n\n## Test contract card\n- authoritative_contract: signed total write-parameter parity ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish plus relation-scoped unlink contract in docs/user-guide.md, docs/cli-reference.md, and test_unlink_relation_scoped_e39f.py.\n- trigger_preconditions: one ordered ticket pair holds `blocks` then `relates_to`; MCP receives `relation=\"blocks\"`.\n- production_path: real FastMCP registration/schema -> `unlink_tickets` -> public `rebar.unlink` -> real git-backed ticket store.\n- test_tier: interface/lifecycle test; a unit test cannot prove live schema binding and persisted edge selection together.\n- observable_postcondition: live schema advertises optional relation; explicit `blocks` removes only blocks and leaves relates_to; omitted relation removes newest relates_to and leaves blocks.\n- negative_control: omit relation and verify the existing pair-scoped fallback is unchanged.\n- collateral_invariants: the unselected edge and reciprocal relation state remain correct.\n- ci_gate: focused interface suite plus make lint and make typecheck.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] MCP unlink_tickets exposes optional relation with the same type/default as rebar.unlink.\n- [ ] A supplied relation is forwarded unchanged and removes exactly that edge while preserving the other relation.\n- [ ] An omitted relation preserves the documented pair-scoped most-recent fallback.\n- [ ] The live MCP schema advertises relation.\n- [ ] The selected interface test is collected, executes without skip/xfail, and is mutation-sensitive to both signature and forwarding omissions.\n- [ ] Focused MCP/link tests pass.\n- [ ] make lint passes.\n- [ ] make typecheck passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"expose and forward optional relation on MCP unlink_tickets"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_unlink_relation.py","reason":"held-out live-schema and persisted relation-selection RED/GREEN oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f5d48bd8-484d-40a0-a6a8-d33dcd35e4dc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["mcp","parity","links"],"ticket_id":"88b9-c847-3a2e-4c63","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP unlink_tickets cannot target a specific relation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["90383280-e042-4193-9a7a-4912ff8b16e4","0639fd5b-bf48-4273-b1cb-c9f445abff5b","f5d48bd8-484d-40a0-a6a8-d33dcd35e4dc","34fca5df-5fad-457b-94dc-de796fb2e88e","572f8b93-8f78-4ba2-b34f-7b7df448d131","f2094dd7-2f63-4e55-bb9e-d75693916043","055261ce-f082-4cff-902f-9738c0bcb8a9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787087319908510002,"uuid":"5000edef-fd0e-4f50-b6f7-6256b5a3a1c7"}